## Why This Is Asked
Tests data governance, multi-tenant isolation, and purge correctness across streaming and batch layers. DEMO: tombstone propagation, per-tenant retention, and auditable data lineage with rollback capability.

## Key Concepts
- Tombstone events for deletions across all paths
- Per-tenant data retention and purge semantics
- Immutable audit logs and data lineage
- Canary rollback and rollback safety checks
- Testing under late data and clock skew

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: emit tombstone and purge
function deleteTenantUserData(tenantId, userId, beforeTs, modelVersion) {
  const tombstone = {type:'tombstone', tenantId, userId, beforeTs, modelVersion, ts: Date.now()};
  eventBus.emit('cca.delete', tombstone);
  // downstream will purge relevant streams and state stores
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify purge completeness across multiple regions and data stores?
- How would you handle partial purges during network or store degradation and ensure audit integrity?

